            desc: 'Spain will be without two key players for their World Cup round-of-32 match against Austria, but Lamine Yamal\'s full fitness is a major positive for La Roja.',
            content: '<p>Spain face a crucial World Cup 2026 round-of-32 clash against Austria at SoFi Stadium in Inglewood, California, on Thursday, July 2, 2026. Despite missing two key players to injury and card accumulation, good news comes from young attacking midfielder Lamine Yamal, who is confirmed fit and ready to start.</p><p>Yamal, once again emerging as one of world football\'s brightest young stars this season, is reported by China.org.cn to be in full fitness and ready to lead Spain\'s attack. His presence is seen as crucial given La Roja\'s possession-based style built around creativity from the flanks.</p><p>According to Football365, Spain\'s coach is expected to maintain the team\'s signature attacking philosophy despite losing two key players in defense and midfield. Analysts predict Austria will adopt a defensive approach relying on quick counterattacks to upset the favored Spanish side.</p><p>The match is an important test for Spain\'s World Cup title ambitions after an impressive group stage campaign. A win over Austria would send La Roja into the round of 16, moving them closer to reclaiming the world championship.</p><p>Tickets for the SoFi Stadium match reportedly sold out quickly, reflecting strong American public enthusiasm for the World Cup 2026 knockout stage, co-hosted across the United States, Mexico, and Canada.</p>',
